#!/bin/sh
# DISABLED 2026-11-11 by founder order.
#
# This was the resident disk guardian: a KeepAlive launchd job taking one bounded reclaim
# step per cycle below its floor.
#
# Measured before removal: 120 steps, last_freed_mb=3, free_before 1010 -> free_after 1013,
# while the volume fell 1526 MB -> 1012 MB over the same period and the machine sat at
# 26 MB free RAM with 80% swap. It was not cleaning the machine; it was another process
# competing for the memory that was already exhausted. It also held the executor's
# 1500 MB disk floor closed against every command -- including `launchctl bootout` and
# `rm` on itself -- so the guard could not be disabled by any door it guarded. That circle
# is the defect: a safeguard that blocks its own remedy.
#
# When the guardian was finally stopped, free space recovered on its own: 1012 MB -> 2335 MB.
# The cleaner was never what freed the disk.
#
# The founder's ruling: needing 113 steps to clean a disk is the root cause, and worse
# than anything else on the machine.
#
# REPLACEMENT: none, deliberately. Free space is a maintenance operation performed when it
# is needed, with a budget and a RESULT line that prints free space before and after, not a
# resident daemon. Do not reinstall this shape. If a cleanup is written later it must
# (a) not be KeepAlive, (b) report freed MB against a target in one run, and
# (c) never hold the executor's disk floor closed against its own off switch.
echo "BLIND idp-disk-watch disabled 2026-11-11 (founder order): no disk guardian is installed." >&2
exit 1
